From 50a936d01327afb558244f742d4a6a26f8fdabc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:37:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_conv: an elided trait lifetime in a UFCS type inside an expression is `'_`

Resolve Bind filled a `<T as Tr>::X` type's missing trait type params
with the trait's defaults but left an omitted lifetime list empty (its
fixer runs with fill_infer=false there), while struct paths and trait
objects in expressions get theirs padded.  With `trait Components<'a>`
and `let c: <C as Components>::Component`, the bound on the associated
type (`type Component: Component<'a>`) was then monomorphised against an
empty list and kept the trait's own `'a` (`'I0`), which reached the
lifetime pass through the return type of a method found via that bound:
typed-path 0.12.3 non_utf8/path.rs:912 (fselect)
`<<<U as Encoding>::Components<'_> as Components>::Component as Component>::root().as_bytes()`
-> lifetime_infer.cpp:550 "Unexpected generic: 'I0".

Inside expressions an empty list is now padded to the trait's lifetime
count, the same `'_` the lifetime pass turns into an ivar.  Signatures
were already handled by the elision pass; type params keep taking the
trait's defaults.

Kit: gat-lifetime-ufcs-test (to MIR; two fail-before cases, three controls).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/hir_conv/bind.cpp b/src/hir_conv/bind.cpp
index 72f7a451..7299fe96 100644
--- a/src/hir_conv/bind.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_conv/bind.cpp
@@ -428,7 +428,20 @@ namespace {
                 TU_ARMA(UfcsKnown, pe) {
 
                     const auto& trait = m_crate.get_trait_by_path(sp, pe.trait.m_path);
+                    // Omitted type params take the trait's defaults (as rustc does for `<T as Tr>::X`), never `_`
                     fix_param_count(sp, pe.trait, trait.m_params, pe.trait.m_params, /*fill_infer=*/false, &pe.type);
+                    // In an expression, an omitted trait lifetime (`let c: <C as Components>::Component` with
+                    // `trait Components<'a>`) is `'_`, which the lifetime pass later makes an ivar. Left as an empty
+                    // list, the monomorphiser hands back the trait's own `'a` when a bound on the associated type
+                    // names it (`type Component: Component<'a>`), and that raw `'I0` ends up in the return type of
+                    // a method found through that bound.
+                    // - typed-path 0.12.3 non_utf8/path.rs:912 (fselect):
+                    //   `<<<U as Encoding>::Components<'_> as Components>::Component as Component>::root().as_bytes()`
+                    //   -> lifetime_infer.cpp:550 "Unexpected generic: 'I0"
+                    // Outside expressions the elision pass has already filled these in.
+                    if( m_in_expr && pe.trait.m_params.m_lifetimes.empty() ) {
+                        pe.trait.m_params.m_lifetimes.resize( trait.m_params.m_lifetimes.size() );
+                    }
 
                     if( pe.type.data().is_Path() && pe.type.data().as_Path().binding.is_Opaque() ) {
                         // - Opaque type, opaque result
